                "Body appreciation and drive for thinness significantly predicted the scores on the EAT-40. Lower scores on body apprecisation and higher scores on drive for thinness predict higher scores on EAT-40. The relationship between EAT-40 and self esteem and general health was negative but not significant statistically. ";
