<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_1103>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "1103";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Self-compassion (SC) directly improved body satisfaction and reduced disordered eating (DE) in women athletes over time, although no indirect effect via body satisfaction was found. Overall, DE and body image remained relatively stable, highlighting persistent vulnerabilities without intervention";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Complex analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Model-based analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_1103>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_1103>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Track_and_field%2C_swimming%2C_diving%2C_soccer>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "The sample lacked diversity (mainly White female athletes), relied on self-report measures, and examined a short 3–4 month period, limiting generalizability and the ability to capture long-term effects";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "Multiple";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Future research should include more diverse samples, additional body image dimensions, and longer longitudinal designs to better understand how SC influences DE over time and across different athlete populations";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "χ2198 = 1655.32, p < .0001, CFI =.950; TLI =942; RMSEA =.066, 90 % CI [.063–.069] Self-compassion T1-body satisfaction T1 𝛃=.42, p<.001 Body satisfaction T1-disordered eating T1 𝛃=-.79, p<.001 Self-compassion T1-disordered eating T1 𝛃=-.47, p<.001 Self-compassion T1-self-compassion T2 𝛃=.75, p<.001 Self-compassion T1-body satisfaction T2 𝛃=.07 Self-compassion T1-disordered eating T2 𝛃=-.08, p<.05 Body satisfaction T1-body satisfaction T2 𝛃=.60, p<.001 Body satisfaction T1-disordered eating T2 𝛃=-.03, NS Disordered eating T1-body satisfaction T2 𝛃=-.10, p<.05 Disordered eating T1-disordered eating T2 𝛃=.58, p<.001 Self-compassion T2-body satisfaction T2 𝛃=.30, p<.001 Body satisfaction T2-disordered eating T2 𝛃=-.50, p<.001 Self-compassion T2-disordered eating T2 𝛃=-.21, p<.001 R²=.40";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "NA";
