<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_1110>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "1110";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "A factor that significantly increases the risk of developing ED symptoms is the pressures that come from the sport environment regarding the achievement of a low weight and a lean shape. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Complex analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Regression";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_1110>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_1110>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/gymnastics_%28artistic%2C_rhythmic%2C_trampoline%2C_tumbling%2C_aerobic%2C_acrobatic%29>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "The cross sectional design makes it impossible to demonstrate a causal relationship between the variables studied. Self reported questionnaires were used for data collection, which may have increased the risk of producing socially acceptable responses. An eating disorder diagnostic assessment was not performed. It was chosen to include athletes from different disciplines of gymnastics and not only by the more widely studied disciplines of artistic and rythmic gymnastics; it is common that artistic and rhythmic gymnastics are considered disciplines with higher training demands and weight pressures than the rest of the disciplines. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "One";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Interventions should aim to improve the awareness of coaches, judges and sports officials regarding the impact that low weight pressures have on the physical and psychological health of young gymnasts. All adolescents should be offered body composition and nutritional assessment by a registered dietetian. Counseling from mental health experts is crucial in helping athletes feel confident regarding their body appearance and their performance capabilities, as well as giving psychological counseling to those who present symptoms of eating disorders. \nFuture research could include males. Factors such as influence of family and social media should also be adressed. Perceptions of coaches regarding ideal weight, dieting practices and their attitudes towards athletes could also be included in future investigations. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "\nPressures from coaches and sports about weight-eating disorders 𝛃=.217, p=.008\nPressure regarding appearance and performance-eating disorders 𝛃=.449, p<.001\nBMI 𝛃=-.447, p<.001\nR²adjusted=.303";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "NA";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sampleSizeMobilized>
                "147";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportPracticeType>
                "Individual sport";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/typeOfAnalysis>
                "Multiple regression" .

