                "Cross-sectional design, precluding examination of the directionality of the associations between SPA and DEAB. This study focused on the use of DEAB as a coping strategy for physical self-presentational concerns related to thinness or leanness. The fact that this study fails to consider concerns specifically related to muscularity and their possible relation with DEAB is an important limitation. No distinction was made for sports where the main emphasis is on muscularity, weight gain, or even drastric weight control (e.g., body building, football, power lifting). Less than half of the adolescents were involved in competitive sports and most did so at a nonelite level. We cannot identify the moderating role of the type of competition on the relationship between SPA and DEAB. This study neglected to examine more pathogenic behaviors (i.e., fasting, use of laxatives and/or diuretics, enemas, appetite suppressants) that adolescents could use to their physique. We do not know whether SPA is associated with the pathogenic weight control behaviors that adolescents engage in or whether sport practice is a moderator of this relationship. ";
