                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Rowing>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "The SCOFF scale should be complemented by other ED questionnaires to obtain more specific information regarding to ED psychopathology. Small size of the sample also may be a limitation. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "One";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "More research is needed on the key protective/facilitating factors against the development of DE in order to tailor prevention and intervention programmes for athletes, coaches, parents and technical staff, and to ensure that sports policies include health professionals (psychologists, nutritionists of physiotherapists) who are aware of ED. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "Physical self-concept related to attractiveness 𝛃=-.37, p<.01\nPressures from teammates and due to the uniform 𝛃=.17, p<.05\nPsychological well-being autonomy 𝛃=-.18, p<.01\nPhysical self-concept related to strength 𝛃=.18, p<.01\nAge 𝛃=-.10, N.S.\nR²=.35\nAdjusted R²=.33, p<.01";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "NA";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sampleSizeMobilized>
                "206 (total sample)";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportPracticeType>
                "Individual sport";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/typeOfAnalysis>
                "Multiple regression" .

