<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_1484>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "1484";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Adolescent athletes show higher alexithymia and more negative body image than adults, with strong links between emotional expression difficulties, body dissatisfaction, and eating attitudes. The findings highlight the need for early psychological screening and holistic health approaches in athletes";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Simple analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Correlation";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_1484>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_1484>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Football%2C_track_and_field%2C_volleyball%2C_taekwondo%2C_wrestlers%2C_fitness>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "The cross-sectional design prevents causal conclusions, and some relevant factors (e.g., stress) were not assessed. Reliance on self-report data and limited scope may also reduce the accuracy and generalizability of the findings";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "Multiple";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Future studies should use longitudinal and qualitative methods to explore influences such as social media, family support, and sport-specific pressures. Early monitoring and targeted interventions could help prevent the progression to more severe eating disorders";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "r=.033, p=.634";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "NS";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sampleSizeMobilized>
                "206";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportPracticeType>
                "Mixed sport";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/typeOfAnalysis>
                "Pearson correlation" .

