<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_1644>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "1644";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Correlation obtained between anxiety (both trait and state) and the EAT-40 was positively and statistically significant. In the multiple regression analysis that was performed with SCOFF scores as a dependent variable, the most predictive variable was socially prescribed perfectionism. It showed negative correlation with EAT-40 and self esteem. Self esteem is probably a protective factor to develop an eating disorder despite perfectionism, which is the most predictive variable as the multiple linear regression showed, and this variable was high in athletes. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Simple analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Correlation";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
