        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Gender role stress (GRS) and sociocultural influences are impoortant correlated of muscle dysmorphia. Physical unattractiveness explained the greater variance in muscle dysmorphia symptoms of both Female and male. MD symptoms for male were associated with seeing beautiful Female or handsome male in movies, TV, or ads. MD symptoms in male were not related to remarks by male friends or remarks by Female friends. Remarks from male friendss and strangers were more predictive sociocultural influences of MD for Female. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Complex analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Regression";
