<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_189>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "189";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Symptom endorsement does not relate to dance involvement by itself, but rather to involvement in dance classes that teach and emphasize thinness";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Complex analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Regression";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_189>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_189>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "Sample was not a clinical sample. We did not show that dance class-related learning was related to diagnosable dysfunction. The study was cross-sectional and so does not constitute a test of the temporal or causal aspect of the proposed influences of dance class-related learning or of expectancy theory. Our measures of thinness-related learning in dance class was retrospective, so those learning reports may thus be subject to recall bis. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "One";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Research is needed whcich uses objective measures of thinness-related learning in dance class, such as behavioural observations of dance instructors, to begin to untangle the roles of actual learning experiences, individual perceptions and personality dispositions in the relationship between reported learning experiences and eating disorder symptoms. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "R²=.35, p<.001\nTime spent in dance class 𝛃=.01, ns\nLearning regarding thinness 𝛃=.06, ns\nThinness/restricting expectancies 𝛃=.62, p<.001";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "NA";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sampleSizeMobilized>
                "501";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportPracticeType>
                "Individual sport";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/typeOfAnalysis>
                "Hierarchical multiple regression" .

