<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_2083>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "2083";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Results indicated a moderate, positive and significant relationship between evaluative concerns and disordered eating. The associations of striving with the dimensions of eating psychopathology were both weak and one was non-significant. For each group, evaluative concerns was found to have a significant, positive association with the EAT and EDI-BD. Team/individuals athletes have significant positive associations between evaluative concerns and eating/body attitudes while aesthetic athletes had non-significant association between these variables. Regarding striving, team/indivdiual athletes maintained marginally-significant relationships between this dimension of perfectionism and the EAT, while aesthetic athletes maintained a non-significant association between the two variables. There is no relationship between striving and body dissatisfaction for team/indivdiual athletes. Aesthetic athletes displayed a significant negative association between striving and EDI-BD. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Simple analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Correlation";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_2083>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_2083>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance%2C_cheerleading%2C_diving%2C_equestrian%2C_synchronized_swimming%2C_crew%2C_cross_country%2C_skiing%2C_swimming%2C_track_and_field%2C_basketball%2C_field_hockey%2C_ice_hockey%2C_lacrosse%2C_rugby%2C_soccer%2C_squash%2C_tennis%2C_ultimate_frisbee%2C_volleyball>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "The data was collected exclusively at colleges with an NCAA Division III program. This lower level of competition may have affected the results. The sample size was small. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "Multiple";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Future studies may replicate the current methods aong a more competitive population as the degree of competitiveness enforced and internalized by athletes has been highlighted as an important predictor for the development of maladaptive psychological symptoms. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "r=.295, p<.001";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "+";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sampleSizeMobilized>
                "478";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportPracticeType>
                "Mixed sport";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/typeOfAnalysis>
                "Correlation" .

