<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_2088>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "2088";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Results indicated a moderate, positive and significant relationship between evaluative concerns and disordered eating. The associations of striving with the dimensions of eating psychopathology were both weak and one was non-significant. For each group, evaluative concerns was found to have a significant, positive association with the EAT and EDI-BD. Team/individuals athletes have significant positive associations between evaluative concerns and eating/body attitudes while aesthetic athletes had non-significant association between these variables. Regarding striving, team/indivdiual athletes maintained marginally-significant relationships between this dimension of perfectionism and the EAT, while aesthetic athletes maintained a non-significant association between the two variables. There is no relationship between striving and body dissatisfaction for team/indivdiual athletes. Aesthetic athletes displayed a significant negative association between striving and EDI-BD. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Complex analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Regression";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_2088>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_2088>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
