        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "2198";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Higher body image (BI) was associated with lower muscle dysmorphia (MD), suggesting a protective role of positive body perception in weightlifters. While overall BI and MD did not vary by most demographics, BMI and age influenced specific MD symptoms, highlighting nuanced risk patterns";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Simple analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Correlation";
