        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "Societal weight pressures were not exmained. Self report nature of the surveys and the willingness of athletes to honestly and accurately respond to survey items. The results are also based on a conveniance sample of skaters limited to clubs in the Midwest and Northeast. Cross sectional design, causal relationships and change over time could not be determined. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "One";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Sport psychology practiitioners should aid this effort by teaching skaters to appreciate body strengths and utilize psychological skills that may buffer the impact of negative weight pressures (e.g., utilizing positive self talk and realistic goal-setting). \nA random and more representative sample of skaters nationally and internationally, inclusive of males, should be considered in future research. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "r=.40, p<.01";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "+";
