        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "We utilized a convenience sample of Female college students ; no representative of the national population of Female college students as geographical, ethnic and other differences. Data were self reported and some participants may not have disclosed truthful information for different reasons (i.e., denial of eating disturbances, social bias). Athletes with high relative prevalence of DE were not represented in our sample because the university did not have such teams at the time of the study. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "Multiple";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Independent of family history of eating disorders and emotion regulation difficulties, characteristics of Female college athletes should be examined further to identify potential mediators through which athletic status serves as a protective measure from DE risks. Further investigate potential correlates and predictors of DE with large and representative samples of Female athletes that would allow for comparison by types of sport. ";
