<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_2370>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "2370";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Only the personality traits conscientiousness, emotional stability and agreeableness are significantly associated with disordered eating. Our mediation analyses revealed the relationship between conscientiousness and disordered eating was completely mediated via the path of exercise dependence and obsessive compulsive symptoms, while the relationship of emotional stability and disordered eating was partly mediated via exercise dependence symptoms and obsessive compulsive symptoms. Moreover the relationship between agreeableness and disordered eating was only mediated by the severity of obsessive compulsive symptoms. The results of the correaltion analysis revealed that conscientiousness, emotional stability and agreeableness were negatively associated with the severity of disordered eating. In contrast, extroversion and openness to experience did not show a significant association with ED. The multiple mediation model of conscientiousness on disordered eating revaled an indirect effect of conscientiousness on disordered eating via higher exercise dependence symptoms and higher obsessive compulsive symptoms. The multiple mediation model of the effects of emotiona stability on disordered eating demonstrated an indirect effect of emotional stability via exercise dependence and obsessive compulsive symptoms. Considering the single mediation model of agreeableness on disordered eating, our results showed that the relationship between agreeableness and disordered eating can be explained through obsessive compulsive symptoms. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Complex analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Model-based analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_2370>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_2370>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Aerobic_and_anaerobic_exercise>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "This cross sectional study design did not allow conclusions concerning the causal relationship. Symptoms of disordered eating were considered but we did not distinguish between different types of eating disorders, which may limit the generalizabiliy. Only Chinese Female exercisers were included. The inclusion of personality traits was operationalized by using the well etablished big five personality model. However, given that personality traits (e.g., perfectionism) were also identified as core characteristics among these disorders";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "Multiple";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Other personality dimensions or mechanisms should be examined in future studies to allow for more robust and nuanced conclusions. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "Direct effect\nAgreeableness-exercise dependence 𝛃=-.007, N.S.\nExercise dependence-obsessive compulsive 𝛃=.292, p<.05\nObsessive compulsive-disordered eating 𝛃=.345, p<.05\nExercise dependence-disordered eating 𝛃=.025, N.S.\nAgreeableness-obsessive compulsive 𝛃=-.118, p<.05\nAgreeableness-disordered eating 𝛃=-.137, p<.05\nAgreeableness-disordered eating indirect effect 𝛃=-.041, N.S.\nIndirect effect\nAgreeableness-disordered eating direct effect 𝛃=-.137, LLCI=-.177, ULCI=-.022\nAgreeableness-exercise dependence-disordered eating 𝛃=-.000\nAgreeableness-obsessive compulsive-disordered eating 𝛃=-.041, LLCI=-.088, ULCI=-.001\nAgreeableness-exercise dependence-obsessive compulsive-disordered eating 𝛃=-.001\nTotal effect 𝛃=-.130";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "NA";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sampleSizeMobilized>
                "295";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportPracticeType>
                "Individual sport";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/typeOfAnalysis>
                "Mediation analyses" .

