        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "Body satisfaction and eating disorder risk were assessed using a self-assessment method, therefore the participants subjective interpretation of the questions may have influenced the results. The EAT-26 is a screening tool biased toward the thin body ideal and may not detect the risk of some types of ED. ";
