<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_318>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "318";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "This longitudinal study contributes to understanding of the relationship between poor body image and eating psychopathology over time, and across sporting sub-samples (competitive, non-competitive and sports non-engagers). Poor body appreciation and better appearance-related sporting body image predicted eating psychopathology for the whole sample.";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Simple analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Regression";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_318>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_318>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Running%2C_cycling%2C_swimming%2C_hiking%2C_gymgoer_HIIT%2C_gymgoer_weights%2C_gymnastics%2C_dance%2C_crossfit>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "The longitudinal analysis were under-powered and could not be conducted separately for each group. The sample had a majority of females, meaning that any gender-specific regression analysis would have been underpowered for males. The age range was wider than in other studies and individuals engaged in a range of different sports, which might have impacted findings. The measures might not have been the optimum set. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "Multiple";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Futures studies could recruit different samples to explain the body image-eating psychopathology link, such as all genders and gender identities and other sports types. Ethnicity should also be considered, given the fact that the thin-ideal is differently experienced in different groups. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "𝛃=.79, N.S.\nR=.79, N.S.\nR²=.63, p<.001\nR²change=.63\n";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "NS";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sampleSizeMobilized>
                "230";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportPracticeType>
                "Mixed sport";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/typeOfAnalysis>
                "Simple linear regression" .

