<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_320>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "320";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Athletes are susceptible to negative mental-health outcomes, better support systems are warranted to protect them from the harmful effects of eating disorders, and to support those who may already be sttruggling. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Simple analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Correlation";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_320>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_320>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Swimming%2C_cross_country%2C_dance%2C_soccer%2C_volleyball%2C_field_hockey%2C_badminton%2C_frisbee%2C_basketball%2C_football%2C_rugby%2C_lacrosse>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "Athletes were aware of the nature of this research as they were informed about what we were studying prior to participation. Participation was voluntary and this may provoked individuals with personal experience with eating disorder behaviours to participate in the research, and discouraged those who were uninterested in the topic from completing the survey. This could change the perceptage and number of participant's concerning results. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "Multiple";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Receive professional education centred around other areas (including sexual violence and substance use), may benefit from increased training around eating behaviours, body image, and mental health. Universities can inregrate student resources within athletics to ensure that athletics are a positive activity for those who participate. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "r=.694, p<.001";
