<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_355>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "355";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "This study highlights gender differences in muscle dysmorphia (MD) symptoms among powerlifters, with men showing higher symptom levels and women experiencing greater body-related distress. Self-esteem, social media comparisons, and performance emerge as key associated factors.";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Complex analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Model-based analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_355>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_355>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Powerlifter>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "The cross-sectional design limits causal inference, and the small, non-representative sample—particularly among women—reduces generalizability. Potential selection bias and reliance on self-reported data also affect validity.";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "One";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Future longitudinal and cross-cultural studies with larger samples are needed. Interventions targeting self-esteem, media literacy, and performance-related pressures may help reduce MD risk in athletes.";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "Depression anxiety and stress 𝛃=.62, p<.001 R²=.389 Depression anxiety and stress 𝛃=.24, p=.075 Self esteem 𝛃=-.45, p=.001 Perfectionism 𝛃=.16, p=.144 Social phobia 𝛃=-.01, p=.930 Instagram appearance comparison 𝛃=.10, p=.357 Objective performance indicators 𝛃=-.20, p=.046 R²=.604";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "NS";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sampleSizeMobilized>
                "53";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportPracticeType>
                "Individual sport";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/typeOfAnalysis>
                "Multiple regression analysis" .

