                "The study show that autonomous motivation for sport had a significant, indirect and positive association with drive for muscularity via perceived behavioral control and intention to gain muscle, and that contolled motivation for sports was related to drive for muscularity both directly and via attitude and intention to gain muscle mass. These results indicate that the trans contextual model was partially supported in the context of bodybuiling, suggesting a complex motivational model underlying drive for muscularity in male bodybuilders. ";
