<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_40>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "40";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Protective and facilitative role of self-compassion in body appreciation, intuitive eating, disordered eating, compulsive exercise, and self-criticism for Canadian Female athletes";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Simple analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Correlation";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_40>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_40>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/volleyball%2C_track_and_field%2C_dance%2C_and_cheerleading>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "An updated version of the BAS was published after all study data had been collected.";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "Multiple";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "(a) Explore Female athletes’ self-compassion, body and eating attitudes and behaviors overtime and within specific sport and international cultural contexts.\n(b) it is unclear how body appreciation and intuitive eating are related to sport performance.";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
