<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_476>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "476";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Satisfaction of psychological need in sport was positively and significantly related to restrictive eating. The results revealed a full mediation effect of self-determination for sport in the association between frustration of psychological need in sport and restrictive eating behaviors. There is a significant negative association between self-determination for sport and restrictive eating behaviors in adolescent athletes. Being an elite athlete did not predict restrictive eating behaviors in our sample. Psychological needs frustration in sport more strongly predicts restrictive eating behaviors in girls, compared with boys. No significant moderation effect of gender was found in the association between satisfaction of psychological need and restrictive eating behaviors. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Complex analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Regression";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_476>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_476>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Endurance%2C_power%2Ftechnical%2C_ball_game%2C_weight_dependent%2C_technical%2C_aesthetic%2C_high_mass>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "First, the associations found between variables do not demonstrate any causal link because the cross-sectional design does not permit any inference about causality. This study used a large and diverse sample, it was not representative of all adolescents in the country, limiting the generalizability of the findings. In addition, problematic eating behaviors in this study refer to restrictive eating, measured by dietary restriction subscale of the EDE-Q. Therefore, the results cannot be extrapolated to other eating behavior problems, such as compulsive eating or binge eating. Moreover, since the instruments used to measure basic psychological needs in sport and self determination for sport were adapted slightly for the sport context by the research team, further studies should replicate these findings using other measures of these contructs. Lastly, constructs were tested with self-reported measures, and therefore, the results may have been influenced by social dsirability. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "Multiple";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Profesionals who guide young athletes in the regulation of their eating behaviors may benefit from more thorough consideration of self-determination and psychological needs specifically in the sport context. Moreover, both frustration and satisfaction of psychological needs in sports should be investigated because restrictive eating was associate with greater satisfaction of psychological needs in the present study. Thus, frustration of psychological needs in sport may be a better indicator of restrictive eating behaviors, especially in girls. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "Chi²(df)=9.85(5), CFI=.98, TLI=.94, RMSEA=.033 [.000-.063]\nBasic psychological needs frustration in sport-self determination in sport 𝛃=-.31, p<.01\nBasic psychological needs frustration in sport-restictive eating behaviors 𝛃=.11 (direct effect) /𝛃=.05, p<.01 (indirect effect)\nBasic psychological need satisfaction in sport-self determination in sport 𝛃=.26, p<.01\nBasic psychological needs satisfaction in sport-restrictive eating behaviors 𝛃=.14, p<.01 (direct effect) / 𝛃=-.05, p<.01 (indirect effect)\nType of sport practiced-restrictive eating behaviors 𝛃=.21, p<.05\nLevel of competition-restrictive eating behaviors 𝛃=.20\nSelf determination in sport-restrictive eating behaviors 𝛃=-.17, p<.01\nR²=.121";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "NA";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sampleSizeMobilized>
                "983";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportPracticeType>
