<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_544>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "544";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "The coach's leadership style (social support and autocratic) influenced the adoption of DEB in young Female volleyball players. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Complex analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Regression";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_544>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_544>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Volleyball>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "Since responses are subjective, athletes may not have indicated total truthfulness in their responses. In addition, it is noteworthy that the BSQ and EAT-26, although presenting acceptable psychometric indexes for the Brazilian Female population, are not specific for athletes. However, there is still no scientifically validated psychometric tool seeking to evaluate DEB and body dissatisfaction related to thinness in athletes. The lack of evaluation of personality traits (anxiety and perfectionism) in athletes is also a limitation. Another limitation that should be maletioned was the use of a double indirect method to evaluat BF%. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "One";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Future studies with longitudinal or prospective design with male volleyball athletes should be conducted in order to investigate the possible influence of the coach's leadership style in the adoption of DEB. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "Age 𝛃=.07, R²=.01, p=.27\nBody fat percentage 𝛃=.12, R²=.08, p=.001\nBody shape 𝛃=.19, R²=.31, p=.001\nTraining instruction 𝛃=.15, R²=.12, p=.34\nSocial support 𝛃=.18, R²=-.16, p=.02\nReinforcement 𝛃=.16, R²=.13, p=.17\nDemocratic 𝛃=.14, R²=.10, p=.21\nAutocratic 𝛃=.19, R²=.18, p=.01";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "NA";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sampleSizeMobilized>
                "73";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportPracticeType>
                "Team sport";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/typeOfAnalysis>
                "Hierarchical regression" .

