<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_553>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "553";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "In the final model, all variables together explained 17% of the variation in EAT-26 scores. These results suggest that concern with body weight and physical appearance and a high level of psychological commitment to exercise are predictors of unhealthy eating habits in athletes. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Complex analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Regression";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_553>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_553>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Artistic_gymnastics%2C_synchronized_swimming_and_diving>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "One limitation of this study was the small sample size, a fact impairing generalization of the results. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "Multiple";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Future studies that include larger samples and additional aesthetic modalities and that evaluate the influence of others factors on the eating behavior of athletes are needed. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "%body fat 𝛃=.14, R²=.004, p<.73\ncommitment to exercise scale 𝛃=.11, R²=.09, p<.05\nBody shape questionnaire 𝛃=.14, R²=.16, p<.02\nAll variables 𝛃=5.32, R²=.17, p<.01";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "NA";
