<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_578>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "578";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Body dissatisfaction is a strong predictor of eating disorders. There are relationships between body dissatisfaction, eating attitude disorder and perceived stress and negative relationship with self-efficacy. Scores for perceived stress were positively related to eating attitude disorder.";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Complex analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Model-based analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_578>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_578>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Running%2C_jumping%2C_throwing_and_sprint>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "First, by using self-report inventories exclusively, data may be susceptible to selective or erroneous reporting. Second, the cross sectional nature of the study does not permit us to state clearly the causal relationships between the variables. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "Multiple";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "it is crucial to steer them away from unhealthy diet and potentially harmful weight-loss behaviors, providing the support of nutritionists and psychologists for the adoption of health eating and physical activity behaviors. It is also important to engage in these interventions, teachers, coaches and family members, as well as people working in the fashion industries. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "Chi²(5) = 9.23, p = 0.10; CFI = 0.98; RMSEA = 0.05; SRMR = 0.05\nInternal locus of control-Self-efficacy 𝛃=.23, p<.05\nSelf-efficacy-Perceived stress 𝛃=-.44, p<.05\nInternal locus of control-Perceived stress 𝛃=-.11, p<.05\nPerceived stress-body dissatisfaction 𝛃=.41, p<.05\nBody dissatisfaction-eating disorders 𝛃=.39, p<.05";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "NA";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sampleSizeMobilized>
                "300";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportPracticeType>
                "Individual sport";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/typeOfAnalysis>
                "Path analysis" .

