<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_611>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "611";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "The mediation analysis suggests that inadequate relational styles with parents can invaludate the emotional regulation of adolescents and encourage orthorexia behaviours. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Simple analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Correlation";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_611>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_611>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Volleyball%2C_basket>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "First, the use of self-report questionnaires could provide information that is not pure because answers might be affected by social desirability. Another limitation is the cross-sectional nature of the current study. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "Multiple";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Coach and practicioners could incorporate aspects of emotional regulation interventions into practices or as supplemental activities to the season. For example, the coach could incorporate lunches with a sport psychologist, who could discuss emotional regulation tactics with the athletes. Similarly, the coach could incorporate goal-setting activities throughout the season, with a focus on how to set smart goals, and then how to regulate emotions through the challenges of achieving such goals. \nFuture research could verify this model in a multi-time perspective as well as including personality and social variables that can be configured as risk and/or protective factors for the etiology of orthorexia. Finally, a longitudinal persceptive would enable a better exploration, through adolescent development, of the indivdiual differences in terms of both emotional and family variables, mainly in adolescents at risk of compulsive behaviours. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "r=.23, p<.001";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "+";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sampleSizeMobilized>
                "303";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportPracticeType>
                "Team sport";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/typeOfAnalysis>
                "Pearson correlation" .

