<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_721>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "721";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Socially prescribed perfectionism did not explain variance in dietary restraint scores. Self esteem oriented perfectionism was associated with dietary restraint and was related to body dissatisfaction. The current findings show a mediating effect of body esteem weight satisfaction on the relationship between self-oriented perfectionism and dietary restraint. The perfectionist personality would be a contributing factor in dietary restraint required to maintin a low body weight. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Simple analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Correlation";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_721>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_721>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Synchronized_swimming>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "Limitations of the study were linked to self-report measures and the cross-sectional nature of the investigations. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "One";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Future research is needed to gain a fuller understanding of the relationship between these three variable. The use of both self-report measures and interview formats in longitudinal studies must be developed to gain a more precise estimate of the nature and extent of inappropriate compensatory behaviours amog synchronized swimmers. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "r=.49, p<.01";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "+";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sampleSizeMobilized>
                "33";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportPracticeType>
                "Team sport";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/typeOfAnalysis>
                "Correlation" .

