<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_741>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "741";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Social pressure, social support, self esteem, body dissatisfaction was related to DE. Social support was not strongly related to DE.. Activity specific body image dissatisfaction is a better predictor of DE than general body image dissatisfaction. When the pressure to be thin was introduced into the model, the competitive level was no longer significant in predicting aesthetic performers DE. Our final model explained 61% of the variance in aesthetic performers disordered eating and also confirmed the role of low self esteem and specific body image dissatisfaction as partial mediators from pressure to be thin to DE. ";
