<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_750>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "750";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "Parental influences are predictors of low self-esteem and DE only among elite athletes. Body image dissatisfaction corresponds to the strongest predictor of DE in elite athletes but not for non elite athletes. Self esteem was not a predictor of DE in elite athletes, in contrast to the other two groups. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Complex analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Model-based analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_750>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_750>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance%3B_gymnastics>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "Minimum criteria to undertake structural equation models, the small number of male athletes may have skewed the results. The cross sectional design of this study does not permit causal inference. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "Multiple";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Future studies should test the same models with different samples of male and Female athletes to determine the generazibility of these findings. A clinical evaluation of adolescents who reported disordered eating is needed to examine the prevalence of true eating disorders, especially among athletes. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "Chi²(17) = 28.28, p<0.05; SRMR = 0.07; IFI = 0.97; RMSEA = 0.08; R²=.647\nSex-social pressure 𝛃=.22, p<.01\nSex-body image dissatisfaction 𝛃=-.25, p<.01\nBMI-parental influences 𝛃=.19, p<.05\nBMI-self esteem 𝛃=-.22, p<.05\nBMI-body image dissatisfaction 𝛃=-.37, p<.001\nBMI-social pressure 𝛃=.31, p<.001\nSocial pressure-self esteem 𝛃=-.38, p<.001\nSocial pressure-anxiety depression symptomatology 𝛃=.28, p<.001\nSocial pressure-body image dissatisfaction 𝛃=-.30, p<.001\nSocial pressure-disordered eating 𝛃=.42, p<.001\nSelf esteem-overeating 𝛃=-.31, p<.001\nSelf esteem-anxiety depression symptomatology 𝛃=-.43, p<.001\nSelf esteem-disordered eating 𝛃=-.16, p<.05\nBody image dissatisfaction-disordered eating 𝛃=-.24, p<.001\nOvereating-disordered eating 𝛃=.16, p<.05";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
