        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Fitness%3B_crossfit>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "Small number of participants and who were practitioners of only two modalities, which males impossible to generalize th results to practitioners of other exercises. \nThe cross sectional design which does not allow to make inferences of causality between the variables. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "Multiple";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Future researches should extend the study with practitioners from other regions of Brazilian population and exercises. \nA longitudinal study will be able to point to the causal nature of the association between BD, addiction to exercise and risk behavior for ED. \nIt is important that instructors and personal trainers analyse the real motives of the individuals to begin the practice of the exercise, always considering the chosen modality. Moreover, it is essential to emphasize the effects of long term training focusing on maintaining health and quality of life, always respecting the individuality and healthy evolution of training. ";
