<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_882>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "882";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "The severity of appearance-based critical comments, and lower self esteem were associated with heightened eating psychopathology. Critical comments could negatively impact on the dancer's psychological well-being, such as lowering self-esteem, which in turn could increase the risk for eating psychopathology. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Simple analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Regression";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_882>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_882>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "The use of questionnaires, which may underestimate the levels of eating, weight or shape concerns. The cross-sectional design meant that it is impossible to ascertain whther those in the critical comments group had already had heightened eating, weight and shape concerns, which led thme to interprating body weight and shape comments from a teacher as being critical; rather tha the comment itself leading to increased eating psychopatholoy. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "One";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Longitudinal study design. Future research should look to further examine the negative effect of critical comments on dancer's psychological well-being. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "𝛃=.69, p<.001\nR²=.46";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "+";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sampleSizeMobilized>
                "77";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportPracticeType>
                "Individual sport";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/typeOfAnalysis>
                "Simple linear regression" .

