<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_95>
        a       <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Analysis>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/analysisId>
                "95";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/authorConclusion>
                "The current findings support body talk and fat talk as a potential risk factor for eating disorders among male. Muscle-focused body talk may not a risk factor for diagnostic eating disorder symptoms. Muscle talk among male is related less to muscle dissatisfaction and more to male socioalization processes. Athletic identity did non emerge as a significant moderator of the association between body talk and eating disorder symptoms. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/complexityOfAnalysis>
                "Complex analyses";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/groupStatisticalAnalysis>
                "Regression";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasPopulation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_95>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasRelation>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_95>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/hasSport>
                <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Mixed_sport>;
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/limites>
                "The study was limited to a single university campus in the southeastern United States, limiting generalizability of the findings. Few participants endorsed aesthetic or lean sports, potentially attenuating results. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/numberOfSportStudied>
                "Multiple";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/perspectives>
                "Future work may benefit from using a more objective of body composition. \nFuture work should explore such associations among male in a clinical sample, examining whether fat or muscle talk is associated with eating disorder and/or muscle dysmorphia symptom severity. \nFat talk may be an important prevention target amon male, regardless of athletic identity. ";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDegree>
                "Model 2\nAge 𝛃=.08, p=.137\nBMI 𝛃=.12, p=.058\nMuscle Talk 𝛃=-.05, p= .424\nFat Talk 𝛃=.60, p<.001";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/relationDirection>
                "NA";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sampleSizeMobilized>
                "224";
        <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportPracticeType>
                "Mixed sport";
