                "This would suggest that resiliency against unhealthy eating could be increased by teaching athletes how to develop and maintain high levels of positive perfectionism. Intervention with goal in mind is a worthy topic for future research. \nDo these perfectionistic tendencies change throughout an athlete's career ? How and why do these changes occur ? What implications do these changes have on eating attitude ?";
